# Contributing to {{.ProjectName}}

Thank you for your interest in contributing! Here's how to get started.

## Getting Started

1. Fork the repository
2. Clone your fork: `git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/{{.ProjectName}}.git`
3. Create a branch: `git checkout -b feature/your-feature`
{{- if eq .Language "Go"}}

### Go Development Setup

```bash
# Install dependencies
go mod download

# Run tests
go test ./...

# Build
go build ./...

# Lint (requires golangci-lint)
golangci-lint run
```
{{- else if or (eq .Language "JavaScript") (eq .Language "TypeScript")}}

### Node.js Development Setup

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Run tests
npm test

# Build
npm run build

# Lint
npm run lint
```
{{- else if eq .Language "Python"}}

### Python Development Setup

```bash
# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Run tests
pytest

# Lint
flake8
```
{{- else if eq .Language "Rust"}}

### Rust Development Setup

```bash
# Build
cargo build

# Run tests
cargo test

# Lint
cargo clippy
```
{{- end}}

## Making Changes

1. Make your changes
2. Write or update tests
3. Ensure all tests pass
4. Commit with a descriptive message (we use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/))

## Pull Request Process

1. Update documentation if needed
2. Add a changelog entry if applicable
3. Submit a pull request with a clear description

## Code of Conduct

Please read our [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) before contributing.
